# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep stray private material out of the repository (THE-72).
#
# Three layers, in this order (a later rule wins):
#   1. Score, audio and archive types are ignored everywhere by extension.
#   2. Five directories that legitimately track such files re-include them.
#   3. Executables, installers and secrets are ignored everywhere again, so the
#      re-includes can never expose a key, an .env file or a binary.
# Ignoring never un-tracks a file that is already committed, and the re-includes
# cover every location that tracks one today, so
# `git ls-files -ci --exclude-standard` lists nothing new. To add a fixture, put
# it in one of the re-included directories (or add a path-scoped "!" rule here
# and the matching entry in scripts/secret-scan.mjs). Never commit private
# scores, extracted binaries or generated test output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Scores and exchange formats (the formats src/interchange reads and writes)
*.gp
*.gp3
*.gp4
*.gp5
*.gp8
*.gpx
*.gpif
*.ptb
*.tg
*.tabplayer
*.musicxml
*.mxl
*.mid
*.midi

# 1. Audio
*.wav
*.mp3
*.ogg
*.flac
*.m4a
*.aif
*.aiff
*.nam

# 1. Archives
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tgz
*.gz

# 2. Legitimate locations that track files of the types above
!/assets/library/**
!/src-tauri/resources/cabinet-irs/**
!/src-tauri/tests/fixtures/**
!/src/interchange/fixtures/**
!/tests/fixtures/**

# 3. Executables, installers and plug-ins: ignored everywhere
*.exe
*.msi
*.dmg
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.vst3

# 3. Secrets and signing keys (including the Tauri updater signing key): ignored everywhere
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.p8
*.jks
*.keystore
.tauri/
